  "grammar": {
    "title": "Plural Nouns: Regular and Irregular",
    "explanation": "We use plural nouns when we talk about more than one thing. One **ear**, two **ears**.\n\nFor most words, we add **s** to make the plural. One finger, two **fingers**.\n\nSome words change in a special way. One **tooth**, two **teeth**. These words do not take **s**.\n\nBe careful: **s** is not always right. We do not say two tooths.",
    "examples": [
      "I have two *ears*.",
      "She brushes her *teeth* every day.",
      "He has ten *fingers*.",
      "My *knees* are strong.",
      "They carry bags on their *shoulders*.",
      "One *tooth*, two *teeth*."
    ],
